From: Matthew Bodenham <matthew@bodenham.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:05:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?x1600:=20VMStateDescription=20on=20every=20cust?=
 =?UTF-8?q?om=20device=20=E2=80=94=20migration=20snapshots=20work?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The machine's custom devices were the only unmigrated state: a migrate/
loadvm restored RAM + the CPU but reset every custom MMIO block, so the
resumed guest ran with reset devices behind its live drivers (the DHD's
staged control response gone, the SFC page cache empty, RTC/CGU back at
seed, GPIO pending bits cleared). Every custom device now carries a
VMStateDescription (version_id 1):

- OST: regfile + period + the armed clockevent deadline (VMSTATE_TIMER_PTR;
  the free-running counter derives from QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL, re-based by
  the stream).
- CGU: regfile + the CE-trigger written bitmap.
- MSC x2 (instance ids 0/1): host regfile, staged RES byte window,
  CCCR/CIS, fn1/fn2 windows, staged CMD53 phase, staged chip-side
  control response (fn2_rd + ctl_stage), the PA08 re-kick timer, and
  the backplane windows — moved from heap chunks to inline
  bp_windows[16][0x8000] (claim zero-fills exactly like the old
  g_malloc0; bp_keys[] with X1600_MSC_BP_FREE sentinels) so the state
  snapshots. post_load recomputes the IRQ level.
- AIC: regfile + FIFO contents/levels + capture counter + window-snapshot
  latch + the 1 ms drain timer. The capture FILE* stays runtime state
  (X1600_AIC_CAPTURE re-opened by realize; the capture file is external).
- PDMA: regfile + armed chains + irqbit snapshots + the AIC PCM pump
  position and prev-window tracking.
- INTC (QOM device, dc->vmsd): ISR/IMR banks; post_load re-drives the
  CPU line.
- RTC / SADC (post_load re-drives the IRQ) / GPIO (post_load re-drives
  the four bank lines) / EFUSE: regfiles + the model-driven state.
- I2C1+cst8xx: regfile, staged tx/rx, slave latch, sleep-arm, touch
  latch, INT level + re-assert timer.
- LCD: regfile + backend_seen + the fb timer (the surface/fb copy are
  runtime-rebuildable; the restored screendump is byte-identical).
- SFC: control window + CDT + page cache + feature regs + PIO counters;
  the NAND array stays the shared image file (the restore re-mmaps the
  same nand-r1.bin; no file handle migrates); post_load re-drives the IRQ.
- Every stub regfile (sequence instance ids; creation order is
  machine-deterministic): zero-restore would have rewound the USB-PHY
  sequence and the PWM backlight level behind the running guest.

The lazily-created LCD fb timer and the I2C INT re-assert timer are
created eagerly in x1600_mach_init (no functional change) so a restore
side always has them for VMSTATE_TIMER_PTR. post_load hooks only run on
the migration-load path.

Verified: boot -> picker (~33 s wall), stop, migrate file: (57 MB
stream), quit, -incoming file:, cont — the restored screendump is
byte-identical to the pre-save dump and a QMP tap at the English row
advances the wizard; the boot gate compares with zero diffs against the
committed v0.88 baseline (no re-record).
